{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-105792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\times (2F-G)$ at the point $(0,-1,2)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={e}^{x}\\,i+yz\\,j,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=z\\,i+(x+2y)\\,k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F-G) & =∇\\times (2F)+∇\\times (-G) \\\\  & =2∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {e}^{x} & yz & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{x})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x})]k \\\\  & =(0-y)i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-y\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F-G) & =2∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =2[-y\\,i]-[z\\,i+(x+2y)\\,k] \\\\  & =-2y\\,i-z\\,i-(x+2y)\\,k \\\\  & =-(2y+z)\\,i-(x+2y)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,-1,2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (2F-G))(0,-1,2) & =-(2(-1)+2)\\,i-(0+2(-1))\\,k \\\\  & =-(-2+2)\\,i-(0-2)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-105792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\,i+j"] ["math" "-j+2\\,k"] ["math" "-k"] ["math" "2\\,k"] ["math" "3\\,i"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105792" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\times (F+G)$ at the point $(0,1,2)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z\\,i+xz\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{z}^{2}\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2}z & xz & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z)]k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)i-(0-{x}^{2})j+(z-0)k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j+z\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j+z\\,k+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{z}^{2}\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,k \\\\  & =-x\\,i+({x}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\,j+(z-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,2),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (F+G))(0,1,2)=-4\\,j+2\\,k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-131438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\,j+\\,k"] ["math" "-4\\,i+2\\,j"] ["math" "-4\\,i+3\\,k"] ["math" "-4\\,j+2\\,k"] ["math" "-\\,j+3\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4\\,j+2\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\times (F+3G)$ at the point $(0,1,-2)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={y}^{2}\\,i+z\\,j+{x}^{2}\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=-3{x}^{2}\\,j-k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+3G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times (3G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F+3∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {y}^{2} & z & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-1)i-(2x-0)j+(0-2y)k \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+3G) & =∇\\times F+3∇\\times G \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k+3[-3{x}^{2}\\,j-k] \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k-9{x}^{2}\\,j-3k \\\\  & =-i-(9{x}^{2}+2x)\\,j-(2y+3)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,-2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F+3G))(0,1,-2) & =-i-(9(0)^{2}+2(0))\\,j-(2(1)+3)\\,k \\\\  & =-i-5\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-105799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-i-5\\,k"] ["math" "-j"] ["math" "2\\,i-j+2\\,k"] ["math" "5\\,i+j-3\\,k"] ["math" "j-2\