{aligned}∇\\times (2F+G) & =2∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =2[xy\\,j+(y-xz)\\,k]+xy\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =2xy\\,j+2(y-xz)\\,k+xy\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =3xy\\,j+(2y-2xz-x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,2,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (2F+G))(-1,2,0)=-6\\,j+5\\,k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-131434" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131434" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6\\,i+5\\,j"] ["math" "-6\\,j+5\\,k"] ["math" "-\\,i+3\\,k"] ["math" "3\\,i-2\\,j"] ["math" "6\\,j+2\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131434" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6\\,j+5\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $∇\\times (F-2G)$ at the point $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2},-1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=xy\\,i+xz\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i-x\\,k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-2G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times (2G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F-2∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ xy & xz & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)]k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)i-(0-0)j+(z-x)k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)\\,i+(z-x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-2G) & =∇\\times F-2∇\\times G \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)\\,i+(z-x)\\,k-2[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i-x\\,k] \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)\\,i+(z-x)\\,k+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+2x\\,k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)\\,i+(z+x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2},-1),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (F-2G))(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2},-1)=-\\,i+k.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" 