eloper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2x & 1 & 0 \\\\ x & 0 & yz\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1(yz)-0(0)]i-[-2x(yz)-0(x)]j+[-2x(0)-1(x)]k \\\\  & =yz\\,i+2xyz\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =⟨yz,2xyz,-x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(y-{x}^{2})⟨z,0,0⟩+⟨yz,2xyz,-x⟩ \\\\  & =⟨z(y-{x}^{2}),0,0⟩+⟨yz,2xyz,-x⟩ \\\\  & =⟨z(2y-{x}^{2}),2xyz,-x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,2,-1) & =⟨(-1)(2(2)-(0)^{2}),2(0)(2)(-1),-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105962" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-105962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-4,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-2,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,0,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,0,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105962" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-4,0,0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,y,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=xyz.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨yz,xz,xy⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ yz & xz & xy \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡z & y & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[(xz)(0)-(y)(xy)]i-[(yz)(0)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)(xy)]j+[(yz)(y)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)(xz)]k \\\\  & =-x{y}^{2}\\,i+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,j+(z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =xyz⟨0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩+⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-xyz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩+⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},-xyz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},-xy(z\\operatorname{sin}⁡z-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z),z({y}^{2}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,1,0) & =⟨-1,-(0\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131473" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-131473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,2,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,-2,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-1,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131473" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,1,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨0,x,2\\sqrt{y}⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=y{z}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}},0,1⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,{z}^{2},2yz⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,4,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & {z}^{2} & 2yz \\\\ 0 & x & 2\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[({z}^{2})(2\\sqrt{y})-(x)(2yz)]i-[(0)(2\\sqrt{y})-(0)(2yz)]j+[(0)(x)-(0)({z}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(2{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz)\\,i+0\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(y{z}^{2})⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}},0,1⟩+⟨2{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y},0,y{z}^{2}⟩+⟨2{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz,0,y{z}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,4,1)=⟨6,0,4⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-131472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2,0,4⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-4,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-4,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨6,0,4⟩"] ["math" "⟨6,3,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-131472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨6,0,4⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,0,z⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{x}{y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,0,-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x⟩,\\,∇f=⟨\\frac{1}{y},-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & 0 \\\\ y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & 0 & z\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}(z)-0(0)]i-[\\frac{1}{y}(z)-0(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)]j+[\\frac{1}{y}(0)-(-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}})(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)]k \\\\  & =-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{z}{y}\\,j+\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{y}⟨0,0,-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x⟩+⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,-\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩+⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,1,3) & =⟨-\\frac{1(3)}{(1)^{2}},-\\frac{3}{1},0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105960" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-105960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-3,-3,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-4,-2,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,2,4⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-1,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,0,-2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105960" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-3,-3,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),y,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=1+{z}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z),0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,0,2z⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(\\pi ,1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2z \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z) & y & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-2z(y)]i-[0(0)-2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)]j+[0(y)-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)]k \\\\  & =-2yz\\,i+2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(1+{z}^{2})⟨0,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z),0⟩+⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,(1+{z}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z),0⟩+⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2yz,(1+{z}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)+2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(\\pi ,1,0) & =⟨-2(1)(0),(1+(0)^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi +0)+2(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi +0),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "18229cd5b1da830459cad4f9a1b8fc54f3381c90e0054c7ce9ee275861518a94"} {"question" "q-105894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,-1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,0,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,0,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "q-105894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,-1,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/state.json" "file_sha256" "c55d235e41ae13f96aba62478960e2f63b4a4b2978406a58f24e5a2dab1fc37d"} {"question" "e-8745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\nabla\\times(3\\mathbf{F} + \\mathbf{G})$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = 3x\\,\\mathbf{i} + y^2z\\,\\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}, \\quad (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{G})(x,y,z) = 3y^2\\,\\mathbf{i} + 4z\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/example-8745.json" "file_sha256" "acedac8a0473786c7993472e34908f403a46e3cee4063345572a57021f5c525e"} {"question" "e-8745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\times \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =∇\\times (3F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3x & {y}^{2}z & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x)]k \\\\  & =(0-{y}^{2})i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3[-{y}^{2}\\,i]+[3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k] \\\\  & =-3{y}^{2}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =(3{y}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =4z\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,1,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-1,1,0) & =4(0)\\,j+k=k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/example-8745.json" "file_sha256" "acedac8a0473786c7993472e34908f403a46e3cee4063345572a57021f5c525e"} {"question" "e-8931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) =  \\langle 0, y-z, x-y\\rangle$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z) = x+y.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times \\mathbf F = \\langle 0,\\,-1,\\,0\\rangle, \n\\quad\n\\nabla f = \\langle 1,\\, 1,\\, 0\\rangle,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F)$ at the point $(-1,1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/example-8931.json" "file_sha256" "e137541cf6e4c82acce07d7caacb965219fca3ee022d7afc40c699981104751b"} {"question" "e-8931" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F) = f \\nabla \\times \\mathbf {F}+   \\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & y-z & x-y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (y-z)]\\,i-[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (0)]\\,j+[1\\cdot (y-z)-1\\cdot (0)]\\,k \\\\  & =(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j+(y-z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x+y)⟨0,-1,0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-(x+y),0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,-2x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(-1,1,3) & =⟨(-1)-1,\\,-2(-1),\\,1-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073139/example-8931.json" "file_sha256" "e137541cf6e4c82acce07d7caacb965219fca3ee022d7afc40c699981104751b"}] "usage" {"e-8745" [] "e-8931" []} "basis" 2673 "retractions" [[17592186179478 :question/problem "Calculate $\\nabla\\times(3\\mathbf{F} + \\mathbf{G})$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$, where\n\n$\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = 3x\\,\\mathbf{i} + y^2z\\,\\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}, \\quad (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{G})(x,y,z) = 3y^2\\,\\mathbf{i} + 4z\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}$."] [17592186179478 :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F$\n- $\\nabla \\times (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\times \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (3F + G) &= ∇ \\cdot (3F) + ∇ \\cdot G \\\\\n&= 3∇ \\cdot F + ∇ \\cdot G\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}$. In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot F &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3x & y^{2}z & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= [\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2) - \\frac{∂}{∂z}(y^{2}z)]i - [\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2) - \\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x)]j + [\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y^{2}z) - \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x)]k \\\\\n&= (0 - y^{2})i - (0 - 0)j + (0 - 0)k \\\\\n&=-y^{2}i\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (3F + G) &= 3∇ \\cdot F + ∇ \\cdot G \\\\\n&= 3[- y^{2}i] + [3y^{2}i + 4zj + k] \\\\\n&=-3y^{2}i + 3y^{2}i + 4zj + k \\\\\n&= (3y^{2} - 3y^{2})i + 4zj + k \\\\\n&= 4zj + k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,1,0)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(∇ \\cdot (F - G))(-1, 1, 0) &= 4(0)j + k = k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186179480 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) = \\langle 0, y-z, x-y\\rangle$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z) = x+y$. Given that\n$\\nabla\\times \\mathbf F = \\langle 0,\\,-1,\\,0\\rangle, \\quad \\nabla f = \\langle 1,\\, 1,\\, 0\\rangle$,\ncalculate $\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F)$ at the point $(-1,1,3)$."] [17592186179480 :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F) = f \\nabla \\times \\mathbf {F}+ \\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇f \\cdot F &= \\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & y - z & x - y\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= [1 \\cdot (x - y) - 0 \\cdot (y - z)]i - [1 \\cdot (x - y) - 0 \\cdot (0)]j + [1 \\cdot (y - z) - 1 \\cdot (0)]k \\\\\n&= (x - y)i + (y - x)j + (y - z)k \\\\\n&= ⟨x - y, y - x, y - z⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (fF) &= f∇ \\cdot F + ∇f \\cdot F \\\\\n&= (x + y)⟨0,-1, 0⟩ + ⟨x - y, y - x, y - z⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, - (x + y), 0⟩ + ⟨x - y, y - x, y - z⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨x - y,-2x, y - z⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∇ \\cdot (fF)(-1, 1, 3) &= ⟨(-1) - 1,-2(-1), 1 - 3⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2, 2,-2⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
